<span id="Description"></span>
== Descrizione ==

{{Codeextralink|https://raw.githubusercontent.com/2cv001/3D_printer_3mf_workflow/refs/heads/main/3D_Printer_3mf_Workflow.FCMacro}}

Macro FreeCAD che esporta file 3MF lisciati e conserva tutte le impostazioni di stampa dello slicer, con flusso di lavoro automatico per lo slicer preferito.

Descrizione più dettagliata:

https://github.com/2cv001/3D_printer_3mf_workflow/blob/main/README.md

<span id="Purpose"></span>
=== Scopo ===

Questa macro automatizza e migliora il flusso di lavoro di stampa 3D da FreeCAD al proprio slicer:
* Generazione di stampe 3D lisce senza sfaccettature visibili.
* '''Preserva le impostazioni di stampa (temperatura, supporti, velocità...)''' in modo da mantenerle collegate al progetto FreeCAD.
* Avvio di programmi esterni per semplificare l'intera pipeline: FreeCAD → Slicer → Stampa.

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
== At a glance ==
</div>

<div lang="en" dir="ltr" class="mw-content-ltr">
* '''Smooth prints''': curved surfaces come out without visible facets.
* '''Your slicer settings are kept''': set them once in the slicer (temperature, supports, infill…); every new export from FreeCAD keeps them.
* '''From FreeCAD to the slicer in one click''': the macro exports the 3MF and opens it in your slicer.
* '''Several objects at once''', each one with its own settings.
* '''Your own commands before or after the export''': turn on the printer through a smart plug while FreeCAD exports, preheat, copy the 3MF… Ready-made templates, a live check and a Test button help to write them.
* '''You see what you export''': a preview of the selected objects and the estimated export time.
* '''Works with most slicers''': QIDISlicer, QIDIStudio, PrusaSlicer, OrcaSlicer, Bambu Studio, Cura, Creality Print, Anycubic.
</div>

